  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 0.7.1, package.json says 0.1.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "docs/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Controller/PageController.php:57 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += docs ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: composer.json requires php ^8.2; appinfo/info.xml declares no php dependency.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^24.0.0 (package.json engines.node), 24 (ci.yml).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.mjs), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml).",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json, composer.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, MIT.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 35 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
